HYPOTHESIS EVALUATION
========================================================================================================================

H1 (Periodicity prior gap):
  Best PCR (pcr_alpha0.5): 54.0285 vs Baseline: 52.6795 (delta=+1.3491)
  NOT SUPPORTED: PCR does not reduce test RMSE

H2 (In-training contrastive provides regularization):
  PCR best overfitting gap: 11.3603
  Baseline overfitting gap: 7.4096
  NOT SUPPORTED: PCR does not reduce overfitting

H3 (GIN sufficient per Small-Graph Paradox):
  GIN with 5 layers, hidden_dim=256, mean_pool: 681,478 params
  Baseline test RMSE: 52.6795
  (Reference: Day 1 GIN Trimer was 50.19 with 3 layers)

Domain-specific vs generic augmentation:
  PCR (monomer-trimer pairs): 54.0285
  Random (edge masking): 66.9588
  Domain-specific positive pairs are better by 12.9303

Data augmentation vs contrastive:
  GRIN (augmentation only): 55.1341
  PCR (augmentation + contrastive): 54.0285
  Contrastive adds value beyond data augmentation
